    <string name="settings_erase_title">Erase all data?</string>
    <string name="settings_erase_message">All contacts, card images, tags, follow-ups and your digital card will be permanently deleted from this device. Backup files you saved are not affected. This cannot be undone.</string>
    <string name="settings_erase_confirm">Erase</string>

    <!-- Privacy -->
    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="privacy_intro">VCardly is built to keep your contacts yours. Here is exactly what it does with your data.</string>
    <string name="privacy_stays_title">Your data stays on this device</string>
    <string name="privacy_stays_body">Contacts, card photos, notes, tags, follow-ups and settings are stored in the app\'s private storage on this phone. Other apps cannot read them. Android\'s automatic cloud backup is switched off for this app.</string>
    <string name="privacy_no_account_title">No account</string>
    <string name="privacy_no_account_body">There is no sign-in and no VCardly server. Your contacts are never uploaded. The internet permission exists only for two things: showing ads on the free plan and handling purchases through Google Play. Pro users see no ads.</string>
    <string name="privacy_permissions_title">Permissions and why</string>
    <string name="privacy_permissions_body">Camera: only while you scan a card; photos stay on the device. Notifications: to show your follow-up reminders; on the lock screen they only say "Follow-up reminder". Exact alarms: so reminders arrive on time. Restart: so reminders come back after you restart the phone. Fingerprint and face: only to unlock the app; VCardly never sees your biometric data. Internet: only for ads and Google Play purchases, never for your contacts.</string>
    <string name="privacy_ocr_title">Reading business cards</string>
    <string name="privacy_ocr_body">Text on a card is recognised on the device. The recognised text is never stored or logged: you review it, and only what you save is kept. You can always edit or delete it.</string>
    <string name="privacy_sharing_title">Sharing</string>
    <string name="privacy_sharing_body">Nothing is shared unless you choose to. When you share a QR code or contact file you pick which details go in, and your private notes are never included. Exports and backups are saved to the place you choose.</string>
    <string name="privacy_backup_title">Backups</string>
    <string name="privacy_backup_body">A backup file contains all your contacts. Protect it with a password (recommended): it is then encrypted and cannot be opened without it. We cannot recover a forgotten password.</string>
    <string name="privacy_lock_title">App lock and screen privacy</string>
    <string name="privacy_lock_body">App lock asks for your fingerprint, face or device PIN, and locks again after the time you choose. Hiding content in recent apps keeps your contacts out of the app switcher and screenshots. App lock controls access to the app; it does not add a second layer of encryption to the stored data.</string>
    <string name="privacy_control_title">You are in control</string>
    <string name="privacy_control_body">You can export everything, restore it elsewhere, or erase all data from Settings at any time. Uninstalling the app removes its data from the phone.</string>

    <string name="privacy_ads_title">Ads and purchases</string>
    <string name="privacy_ads_body">The free plan shows one banner ad from Google AdMob on the Home screen. It never appears next to a person\'s details, and VCardly gives the ads no information about your contacts. Google may use your device\'s advertising ID to choose and measure ads, and in some regions asks for your consent first (you can change it in Settings). VCardly Pro removes ads entirely. Payments are handled by Google Play; VCardly never sees your payment details.</string>

